data.content:
In **EF Core 11** (with the Cosmos DB provider), the **sync-over-async opt-in is removed entirely**. All synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`) and `SaveChanges()` on the Cosmos DB provider now throw `InvalidOperationException` — there is no configuration to re-enable them.

**What breaks:** Every method in your repository. The Cosmos SDK is inherently async, and EF Core no longer wraps it.

**Fix — convert to async:**

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

- `Add()` is still synchronous (it's in-memory tracking, no I/O) — only the flush (`SaveChangesAsync`) needs async.
- All callers up the chain must also become `async`/`await` — this typically ripples up to your controllers/endpoints.
- If you have interfaces like `IProductRepository`, update the return types to `Task<T>` as well.
